12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast the structural parameters of B-DNA, A-DNA, and Z-DNA regarding helical handedness, base pairs per turn, pitch, and major/minor groove topologies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Structural Analysis of DNA Polymorphs \(B-DNA, A-DNA, and Z-DNA\):) Tj
T*
(   1. B-DNA \(The Physiological Standard\):) Tj
T*
(   - Helical Handedness: Right-handed double helix.) Tj
T*
(   - Base Pairs per Turn: 10.4 to 10.5 bp per turn in aqueous solution.) Tj
T*
(   - Helical Pitch: 3.4 nm \(34 A\) per turn; axial rise per base pair is 0.34 nm \(3.4 A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Helix Diameter: ~2.0 nm \(20 A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Sugar Pucker: C2'-endo conformation.) Tj
T*
(   - Glycosidic Bond Conformation: Anti conformation for all purine and pyrimidine bases.) Tj
T*
(   - Groove Geometry: Possesses a wide, deep Major Groove \(accessible for sequence-specific) Tj
T*
(   transcription factor binding\) and a narrow, deep Minor Groove.) Tj
T*
(   2. A-DNA \(Dehydrated / RNA-DNA Hybrid Form\):) Tj
T*
(   - Helical Handedness: Right-handed double helix, broader and more compact than B-DNA.) Tj
T*
(   - Base Pairs per Turn: 11 bp per turn.) Tj
T*
(   - Helical Pitch: 2.8 nm \(28 A\); axial rise is 0.26 nm \(2.6 A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Helix Diameter: ~2.3 nm \(23 A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Sugar Pucker: C3'-endo conformation \(forced by steric hindrance of the 2'-OH group in dsRNA) Tj
T*
(   or RNA-DNA hybrids\).) Tj
T*
(   - Base Pair Tilt: Highly tilted relative to the helical axis \(~20 degrees\).) Tj
T*
(   - Groove Geometry: Extremely narrow, deep major groove; very broad, shallow minor groove.) Tj
T*
(   3. Z-DNA \(Left-Handed Alternating Purine-Pyrimidine Form\):) Tj
T*
(   - Helical Handedness: Left-handed double helix with a characteristic zigzag phosphodiester) Tj
T*
(   backbone.) Tj
T*
(   - Sequence Requirement: Requires alternating purine-pyrimidine dinucleotide tracts, most) Tj
T*
(   favorably d\(C-G\)n, stabilized in vivo by negative supercoiling and cytosine C5-methylation.) Tj
T*
(   - Base Pairs per Turn: 12 bp per turn \(repeating unit is a dinucleotide\).) Tj
T*
(   - Helical Pitch: 4.5 nm \(45 A\); axial rise is 0.37 nm \(3.7 A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Helix Diameter: ~1.8 nm \(18 A, the slimmest DNA conformation\).) Tj
T*
(   - Sugar Pucker and Glycosidic Conformation: Alternating! Pyrimidines \(C\) have C2'-endo pucker) Tj
T*
(   and Anti glycosidic bonds; Purines \(G\) have C3'-endo pucker and Syn glycosidic bonds.) Tj
T*
(   - Groove Geometry: Virtually lacks a distinct major groove \(pushed out to convex surface\);) Tj
T*
(   possesses a single very deep, narrow minor groove.) Tj
