(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the molecular architecture of the eukaryotic Replication Fork, detailing the distinct roles of Pol alpha-primase, Pol delta, Pol epsilon, PCNA, RFC, and FEN1.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Eukaryotic Replication Fork Architecture and Lagging Strand Processing:) Tj
T*
(   1. Asymmetric Division of Labor at the Fork:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike the bacterial replication fork where Pol III synthesizes both strands, the eukaryotic) Tj
T*
(   fork utilizes three distinct B-family DNA polymerases:) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Polymerase alpha - Primase Complex: A heterotetrameric complex. Primase synthesizes an) Tj
T*
(   8-10 nucleotide RNA primer; Pol alpha then extends it with 10-20 deoxyribonucleotides,) Tj
T*
(   generating a hybrid RNA-DNA primer before dissociating. Lacks proofreading exonuclease) Tj
T*
(   activity.) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Polymerase epsilon: Possesses high intrinsic processivity and vigorous 3'-to-5') Tj
T*
(   proofreading. Anchored directly to the CMG helicase via its non-catalytic C-terminal domain,) Tj
T*
(   synthesizing the Leading Strand continuously.) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Polymerase delta: A four-subunit enzyme possessing 3'-to-5' proofreading exonuclease) Tj
T*
(   activity. Operates in conjunction with PCNA to synthesize the Lagging Strand discontinuously as) Tj
T*
(   Okazaki fragments \(~150-200 nt\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The Sliding Clamp and Loader \(PCNA and RFC\):) Tj
T*
(   - Proliferating Cell Nuclear Antigen \(PCNA\): A homotrimeric ring with pseudo-sixfold symmetry,) Tj
T*
(   possessing a 34 A central channel encircling double-stranded DNA. Acts as a sliding platform) Tj
T*
(   recruiting polymerases, repair enzymes, and chromatin remodelers.) Tj
T*
(   - Replication Factor C \(RFC\): A pentameric AAA+ ATPase clamp loader that binds PCNA, hydrolyzes) Tj
T*
(   ATP to open the ring, and latches it around primer-template junctions, executing the) Tj
T*
(   'Polymerase Switch' from Pol alpha to Pol delta/epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   3. Okazaki Fragment Maturation \(The FEN1 Pathway\):) Tj
T*
(   - When Pol delta synthesizing an Okazaki fragment reaches the 5'-end of the preceding fragment,) Tj
T*
(   it does NOT stop; it processively displaces the 5'-RNA-DNA primer, creating a transient,) Tj
T*
(   single-stranded 5'-Flap.) Tj
T*
(   - Flap Endonuclease 1 \(FEN1\): Directly recruited to PCNA. FEN1 tracks down the 5'-flap and) Tj
T*
(   endonucleolytically cleaves it at the junction between single- and double-stranded DNA,) Tj
T*
(   removing the error-prone Pol alpha-synthesized primer.) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Ligase I: Recruited to the resulting nick by PCNA, utilizing ATP to synthesize the final) Tj
T*
(   phosphodiester bond, generating a continuous lagging strand.) Tj
T*
