T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The End-Replication Problem and Telomerase Biology:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Biophysical Origin of the End-Replication Problem:) Tj
T*
(   - Replicative DNA polymerases require a pre-existing 3'-OH primer and synthesize DNA) Tj
T*
(   exclusively in the 5'-to-3' direction.) Tj
T*
(   - On the lagging strand, synthesis of the terminal Okazaki fragment requires an RNA primer) Tj
T*
(   positioned at the extreme physical end of the linear chromosome.) Tj
T*
(   - Following synthesis, the terminal RNA primer is removed by RNase H and nucleases.) Tj
T*
(   - Because there is no upstream DNA to provide a 3'-OH template for polymerase elongation, this) Tj
T*
(   terminal gap cannot be filled!) Tj
T*
(   - Consequently, linear eukaryotic chromosomes lose 50 to 100 base pairs of telomeric DNA from) Tj
T*
(   the 3'-lagging strand with every round of somatic cell division \('the End-Replication) Tj
T*
(   Problem'\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Architecture of Telomerase:) Tj
T*
(   Telomerase is a specialized ribonucleoprotein \(RNP\) reverse transcriptase complex consisting of) Tj
T*
