T*
(   3. The Catalytic Elongation Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Annealing\): The single-stranded 3' G-rich DNA overhang of the chromosome binds and) Tj
T*
(   base-pairs with the 3'-portion of the TERC RNA template.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Reverse Transcription\): TERT uses its integral TERC template to synthesize six) Tj
T*
(   deoxyribonucleotides \(dGTP, dTTP\), extending the single-stranded 3'-end of the chromosome by) Tj
T*
(   one TTAGGG repeat.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Translocation\): TERT/TERC shifts forward along the newly synthesized DNA strand,) Tj
