(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the Base Excision Repair \(BER\) pathway, distinguishing between Short-Patch and Long-Patch repair mechanisms.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Molecular Mechanics of Base Excision Repair \(BER\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Physiological Substrates:) Tj
T*
(   BER repairs non-bulky, non-helix-distorting base lesions generated by endogenous cellular) Tj
T*
(   processes: spontaneous cytosine deamination \(producing Uracil\), depurination, reactive oxygen) Tj
T*
(   species \(forming 8-Oxoguanine\), and alkylation \(forming 3-methyladenine\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Step 1: Base Excision by DNA Glycosylases:) Tj
T*
(   - Lesion-specific DNA glycosylases \(e.g., Uracil-DNA Glycosylase - UDG, OGG1\) scan the genome.) Tj
T*
(   - The damaged base is flipped 180 degrees out of the DNA duplex into the enzyme's catalytic) Tj
T*
(   pocket.) Tj
T*
(   - The glycosylase cleaves the N-glycosidic bond linking the damaged base to the deoxyribose) Tj
T*
(   sugar, releasing the free base and leaving an intact Apurinic/Apyrimidinic \(AP\) site.) Tj
T*
(   3. Step 2: AP Site Incision by AP Endonuclease:) Tj
T*
(   - AP Endonuclease-1 \(APE1\) binds the AP site, endonucleolytically cleaving the phosphodiester) Tj
T*
(   backbone immediately 5' to the abasic sugar.) Tj
T*
(   - This generates a single-strand break flanked by a 3'-hydroxyl \(3'-OH\) group and an intact,) Tj
T*
(   chemically blocking 5'-deoxyribose phosphate \(5'-dRP\) group.) Tj
T*
(   4. Divergence into Two Sub-Pathways:) Tj
T*
(   - Sub-Pathway A: Short-Patch BER \(Single-Nucleotide Repair, > 80% of events\):) Tj
T*
(   * DNA Polymerase beta \(Pol beta\) is recruited to the nick.) Tj
T*
(   * Pol beta inserts a single complementary nucleotide into the 3'-OH end.) Tj
T*
(   * Crucially, Pol beta utilizes its intrinsic N-terminal dRP-lyase domain to excise the blocking) Tj
T*
(   5'-dRP residue via beta-elimination.) Tj
T*
(   * The resulting clean nick is sealed by DNA Ligase III in stable complex with XRCC1.) Tj
T*
(   - Sub-Pathway B: Long-Patch BER \(2 to 10 Nucleotide Repair\):) Tj
T*
(   * Operates when the 5'-sugar residue is chemically modified, oxidized, or reduced, making it) Tj
T*
(   resistant to Pol beta lyase cleavage.) Tj
T*
(   * Replicative DNA Polymerase delta or epsilon, supported by the PCNA sliding clamp, performs) Tj
T*
