(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast Global Genome NER \(GG-NER\) and Transcription-Coupled NER \(TC-NER\) regarding damage recognition, molecular factors, and disease phenotypes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Architecture of Nucleotide Excision Repair: GG-NER vs. TC-NER:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physiological Role:) Tj
T*
(   Nucleotide Excision Repair \(NER\) is the primary excision repair pathway for removing bulky,) Tj
T*
(   helix-distorting DNA lesions that physically obstruct base pairing, predominantly UV-induced) Tj
T*
(   cyclobutane pyrimidine dimers \(CPDs\), 6-4 photoproducts, and chemical carcinogen adducts) Tj
T*
(   \(benzo[a]pyrene, cisplatin\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Divergent Lesion Recognition Phase:) Tj
T*
(   - Global Genome NER \(GG-NER\):) Tj
T*
(   * Scans the entire genome, including silent heterochromatin and non-transcribed strands.) Tj
T*
(   * Recognition relies on the XPC - RAD23B complex \(working with the UV-DDB complex:) Tj
T*
(   DDB1-DDB2/XPE\). XPC does not recognize the chemical lesion itself; it senses the localized) Tj
T*
(   helical thermodynamic destabilization and unpaired bases on the opposite uninjured strand!) Tj
T*
(   - Transcription-Coupled NER \(TC-NER\):) Tj
T*
(   * Operates exclusively on the transcribed \(template\) strand of actively expressed genes.) Tj
T*
(   * Requires NO sensor protein; the damage is detected when an actively transcribing RNA) Tj
T*
(   Polymerase II physically crashes into the bulky lesion and stalls irreversibly.) Tj
T*
(   * Stalled Pol II serves as a high-affinity recruitment platform for Cockayne Syndrome proteins) Tj
T*
(   CSB \(an SWI/SNF-like ATPase\) and CSA \(a WD40 cullin-RING ubiquitin ligase component\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Convergence on Core Excision Machinery \(Dual Incision\):) Tj
T*
(   Once recognized, both pathways recruit the ten-subunit General Transcription Factor TFIIH:) Tj
T*
(   - The ATP-dependent helicases of TFIIH, XPB \(3'-to-5'\) and XPD \(5'-to-3'\), unwind ~30 base) Tj
T*
(   pairs around the lesion, creating a stable transcription bubble.) Tj
T*
(   - XPA verifies the presence of abnormal chemical structures, while RPA protects the undamaged) Tj
T*
(   single strand.) Tj
T*
(   - Dual Endonucleolytic Cleavage:) Tj
T*
(   * Structure-specific endonuclease XPG cleaves the phosphodiester backbone 3' to the lesion) Tj
T*
(   \(~2-8 nucleotides downstream\).) Tj
T*
(   * The XPF - ERCC1 heterodimeric endonuclease cleaves 5' to the lesion \(~16-24 nucleotides) Tj
T*
(   upstream\).) Tj
T*
(   - A damaged oligonucleotide of 24 to 30 nucleotides is released.) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Polymerase delta/epsilon and PCNA fill the gap; DNA Ligase I/III seals the nick.) Tj
T*
(   4. Divergent Clinical Phenotypes:) Tj
T*
(   - Defective GG-NER \(Xeroderma Pigmentosum, XP\): Extreme sun sensitivity, severe freckling, and) Tj
T*
(   a > 1,000-fold elevated incidence of lethal skin cancers \(melanoma, squamous cell carcinoma\)) Tj
T*
(   due to somatic mutation accumulation.) Tj
T*
(   - Defective TC-NER \(Cockayne Syndrome, CS\): Normal cancer incidence! Instead, patients present) Tj
T*
(   with severe, fatal neurodevelopmental dysmyelination, dwarfism, bird-like facies, and premature) Tj
T*
(   segmental progeria caused by permanent RNA Polymerase II transcriptional arrest driving) Tj
T*
(   widespread p53-mediated apoptosis in non-dividing neurons.) Tj
T*
