(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Double-Strand Break \(DSB\) Repair: NHEJ vs. Homologous Recombination:) Tj
T*
(   1. Classical Non-Homologous End Joining \(c-NHEJ\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cell Cycle Timing: Active throughout all cell cycle phases \(G0, G1, S, G2\); dominant in G0/G1) Tj
T*
(   where sister chromatids are absent.) Tj
T*
(   - Fidelity: Error-prone; direct ligation of ends frequently involves nucleolytic trimming and) Tj
T*
(   template-independent insertions, introducing small deletions and point mutations.) Tj
T*
(   - Molecular Cascade:) Tj
T*
(   * Step 1: The doughnut-shaped Ku70 - Ku80 heterodimer binds with picomolar affinity to the) Tj
T*
(   exposed blunt or jagged double-stranded DNA ends.) Tj
T*
(   * Step 2: Ku70/80 recruits the DNA-Dependent Protein Kinase catalytic subunit \(DNA-PKcs\),) Tj
T*
(   assembling the active DNA-PK holoenzyme that synapsed the two DNA ends.) Tj
T*
(   * Step 3: Complex end-processing: Artemis endonuclease is activated by DNA-PKcs phosphorylation) Tj
T*
(   to trim non-ligatable hairpins and single-strand overhangs.) Tj
T*
(   * Step 4: The specialized ligase complex DNA Ligase IV - XRCC4 - XLF joins the broken strands.) Tj
T*
(   2. Homologous Recombination \(HR\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cell Cycle Timing: Strictly restricted to S and G2 phases when an identical, undamaged sister) Tj
T*
(   chromatid is available as a repair template.) Tj
T*
(   - Fidelity: High-fidelity, error-free repair.) Tj
T*
(   - Molecular Cascade:) Tj
T*
(   * Step 1 \(End Resection\): The MRN complex \(Mre11-Rad50-Nbs1\) and CtIP initiate nucleolytic) Tj
T*
(   resection, expanded by Exo1 and Dna2 helicase, digesting 5'-strands to expose long 3') Tj
T*
(   single-stranded DNA overhangs \(> 1 kb\).) Tj
T*
(   * Step 2 \(Rad51 Nucleofilament Assembly\): The ssDNA is coated with RPA. BRCA2 displaces RPA,) Tj
T*
(   catalyzing the cooperative assembly of the recombinase Rad51 into a right-handed helical) Tj
T*
(   nucleoprotein filament.) Tj
T*
(   * Step 3 \(Strand Invasion and D-Loop\): The Rad51-ssDNA filament scans the sister chromatid for) Tj
T*
(   homologous sequence, invading the duplex to form a displacement loop \(D-loop\).) Tj
T*
(   * Step 4 \(Synthesis and Resolution\): DNA Polymerase delta extends the invading 3'-end using the) Tj
T*
(   sister chromatid as template. The structure is resolved either by Synthesis-Dependent Strand) Tj
T*
(   Annealing \(SDSA, non-crossover\) or by Double Holliday Junction resolution \(via BTR or) Tj
T*
(   Gen1/Mus81 resolvases\).) Tj
T*
