(   3. Transition to the Open Complex \(RPo / DNA Melting\):) Tj
T*
(   - Without requiring ATP hydrolysis, the holoenzyme undergoes a spontaneous thermodynamic) Tj
T*
(   isomerisation driven by protein conformational change.) Tj
T*
(   - Invariant aromatic residues in Region 2.3 of sigma-70 \(Tyr-430 and Phe-427\) flip the base) Tj
T*
(   Adenosine at position -11 and Adenosine at -7 out of the DNA duplex into hydrophobic pockets of) Tj
T*
(   the protein.) Tj
T*
(   - This base flipping nucleates localized melting of ~14 base pairs between positions -11 and) Tj
T*
(   +3, exposing the single-stranded template strand in the catalytic active site cleft, forming) Tj
T*
(   the transcriptionally competent Open Complex \(RPo\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Abortive Initiation and Promoter Clearance:) Tj
T*
(   - In the open complex, RNA polymerase binds the initial initiating ribonucleoside triphosphate) Tj
T*
(   \(typically ATP or GTP at +1\) and synthesizes short transcripts of 2 to 9 nucleotides.) Tj
T*
(   - However, during early synthesis, the growing transcript collides sterically with the) Tj
T*
(   N-terminal 'sigma-finger' loop \(Region 3.2\), which obstructs the nascent RNA exit channel.) Tj
T*
(   - The polymerase repeatedly releases these short abortive RNA fragments \(2-9 nt\), remaining) Tj
T*
(   stationary at the promoter while reeling in downstream DNA \('DNA scrunching'\).) Tj
T*
(   - When the nascent transcript successfully reaches ~10-12 nucleotides, its growing bulk) Tj
T*
(   mechanically pushes the sigma-finger out of the exit channel.) Tj
T*
(   - Contact between sigma and the core enzyme is disrupted, sigma factor dissociates, and the) Tj
T*
(   core enzyme 'clears' the promoter, transitioning into a highly stable, processive Ternary) Tj
T*
(   Elongation Complex \(TEC\).) Tj
