(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the stepwise assembly of the Eukaryotic Pre-Initiation Complex \(PIC\) for RNA Polymerase II, highlighting the general transcription factors TFIID, TFIIA, TFIIB, TFIIF, TFIIE, and TFIIH.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Stepwise Assembly of the RNA Polymerase II Pre-Initiation Complex \(PIC\):) Tj
T*
(   1. The Core Promoter Elements:) Tj
T*
(   A minimal DNA region required for accurate in vitro initiation, containing combinations of the) Tj
T*
(   TATA Box \(-30\), Initiator element \(Inr, overlapping +1\), Downstream Promoter Element \(DPE, +28) Tj
T*
(   to +32\), and TFIIB Recognition Element \(BRE, -37\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The Classical Stepwise PIC Assembly Cascade:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(TFIID Binding\): The massive ~800 kDa TFIID complex initiates assembly. The) Tj
T*
(   TATA-Binding Protein \(TBP\) subunit binds the minor groove of the TATA box, inserting four) Tj
T*
(   phenylalanines that kink the DNA by 80 degrees, unwinding the double helix and providing a) Tj
T*
(   stereospecific spatial platform. TBP-Associated Factors \(TAFs\) bind Inr and DPE.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(TFIIA Stabilization\): TFIIA binds to the upstream side of TBP and DNA, stabilizing) Tj
T*
(   the TBP-promoter complex and counteracting transcriptional repressors.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(TFIIB Bridging\): A single polypeptide possessing a conserved C-terminal domain that) Tj
T*
(   contacts both TBP and the upstream BRE element, and an N-terminal zinc ribbon that inserts into) Tj
T*
(   the active site cleft of RNA Pol II. TFIIB acts as the precise molecular ruler dictating) Tj
T*
(   transcription start site \(+1\) selection!) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(RNA Polymerase II - TFIIF Recruitment\): TFIIF forms a tight heterodimer that escorts) Tj
T*
(   RNA Pol II into the nascent complex, correctly orienting the catalytic cleft over the promoter) Tj
T*
(   DNA while preventing non-specific DNA binding.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5 \(TFIIE Docking\): Recruited to the complex, binding directly to Pol II and creating the) Tj
T*
(   essential docking surface for TFIIH.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6 \(TFIIH Integration\): A 10-subunit multifunctional general transcription factor) Tj
T*
(   consisting of a 7-subunit core and a 3-subunit CDK-Activating Kinase \(CAK\) module.) Tj
T*
(   3. Open Complex Formation and Promoter Escape:) Tj
T*
(   - The XPB subunit of TFIIH functions as an ATP-dependent 3'-to-5' DNA translocase that grips) Tj
T*
(   downstream DNA and torques it, feeding DNA into the catalytic cleft to melt ~12-15 base pairs) Tj
T*
(   around +1, creating the eukaryotic Open Complex.) Tj
T*
