(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the C-Terminal Domain \(CTD\) Phosphorylation Code of RNA Polymerase II and how it coordinates 5'-Capping, Splicing, and Polyadenylation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The RNA Polymerase II C-Terminal Domain \(CTD\) Code:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture of the CTD:) Tj
T*
(   The largest subunit of human RNA Polymerase II \(RPB1\) possesses a unique, highly conserved,) Tj
T*
(   flexible C-terminal tail consisting of 52 tandem repeats of the consensus heptapeptide) Tj
T*
(   sequence:) Tj
T*
(   Tyr1 - Ser2 - Pro3 - Thr4 - Ser5 - Pro6 - Ser7.) Tj
T*
(   The CTD functions as a dynamic molecular loading dock whose reversible phosphorylation and) Tj
T*
(   prolyl-isomerization state undergo precise spatial-temporal orchestration across the) Tj
T*
(   transcription cycle.) Tj
T*
(   2. Phase 1: Initiation and 5'-Capping \(High Phospho-Ser-5\):) Tj
T*
(   - During PIC assembly, the CTD is completely unphosphorylated.) Tj
T*
(   - Upon open complex formation, CDK7 \(the kinase subunit of TFIIH\) phosphorylates Serine-5) Tj
T*
(   \(pSer-5\) on all heptad repeats.) Tj
T*
(   - pSer-5 serves as a high-affinity binding platform that directly recruits the mRNA 5'-Capping) Tj
T*
(   Enzyme complex \(RNGTT/RNMT\) to the polymerase.) Tj
T*
(   - As soon as the first 20-30 nucleotides of nascent RNA emerge from the exit channel, the) Tj
T*
(   capping enzymes add the 7-methylguanosine \(m7G\) cap to the 5'-triphosphate, protecting the) Tj
T*
(   transcript from 5'-exonucleases and licensing it for downstream processing.) Tj
T*
(   3. Phase 2: Productive Elongation and Splicing \(The Ser-5 to Ser-2 Transition\):) Tj
T*
(   - Following promoter clearance, the phosphatase Ssu72 and Rtr1/RPAP2 selectively) Tj
T*
(   dephosphorylate Ser-5.) Tj
T*
(   - Concurrently, Positive Transcription Elongation Factor b \(P-TEFb, containing CDK9\)) Tj
T*
(   phosphorylates Serine-2 \(pSer-2\) and the elongation factors DSIF and NELF.) Tj
T*
(   - Elevated pSer-2 recruits elongation factors \(SPT6, FACT\) and coordinates cotranscriptional) Tj
T*
(   pre-mRNA splicing by directly binding components of the spliceosome \(U2 snRNP adaptors\) and) Tj
T*
(   serine/arginine-rich \(SR\) splicing proteins, ensuring splicing occurs co-transcriptionally as) Tj
T*
(   introns emerge.) Tj
T*
(   4. Phase 3: Cleavage and Polyadenylation \(High Phospho-Ser-2\):) Tj
T*
(   - Toward the 3'-end of the gene, pSer-2 density reaches its maximum.) Tj
T*
(   - The dense pSer-2 array acts as a specific recruitment platform for the Cleavage and) Tj
T*
(   Polyadenylation Specificity Factor \(CPSF\) and Cleavage Stimulation Factor \(CstF\).) Tj
T*
(   - When Pol II transcribes the AAUAAA signal, CPSF and CstF transfer from the CTD to the) Tj
T*
(   emerging RNA, cleaving the transcript and synthesizing the poly-A tail.) Tj
T*
(   - The phosphatase FCP1 dephosphorylates Ser-2, resetting the naked CTD for the next) Tj
T*
(   transcription cycle.) Tj
T*
