(   - 5' Splice Donor Site: Invariant 5'-GU-3' dinucleotide embedded in consensus /GURAGU.) Tj
T*
(   - 3' Splice Acceptor Site: Invariant 5'-AG-3' dinucleotide preceded by a Polypyrimidine Tract) Tj
T*
(   \(PPT, ~15-20 consecutive U/C residues\).) Tj
T*
(   - Branch Point Sequence: Conserved sequence located 20-50 bp upstream of the 3' site containing) Tj
T*
(   an Invariant Adenosine \(YNYURAY\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The Two Sequential Transesterification Steps:) Tj
T*
(   Nuclear pre-mRNA splicing is executed via two consecutive S_N2-type transesterification) Tj
T*
(   reactions that conserve the total number of phosphodiester bonds \(requiring zero high-energy) Tj
T*
(   ATP bond cleavage for the chemical ligation steps\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(First Transesterification - Lariat Formation\):) Tj
T*
(   * The 2'-hydroxyl group \(2'-OH\) of the invariant Branch Point Adenosine acts as a nucleophile,) Tj
T*
(   attacking the phosphodiester bond at the 5' splice site \(the G of the GU intron boundary\).) Tj
T*
(   * Cleavage occurs at the 5' exon-intron junction, freeing Exon 1 with a terminal 3'-OH group.) Tj
T*
(   * Concurrently, a novel, unusual 2'-5' phosphodiester bond is formed between the 2'-OH of the) Tj
T*
(   branch point adenosine and the 5'-phosphate of the first intron nucleotide \(G\), generating the) Tj
T*
(   circularized 'Lariat' intermediate.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Second Transesterification - Exon Ligation\):) Tj
T*
(   * The newly liberated 3'-OH of Exon 1 acts as a nucleophile, attacking the phosphodiester bond) Tj
T*
(   at the 3' splice site \(immediately following the AG dinucleotide\).) Tj
T*
(   * The two exons are covalently joined via a standard 3'-5' phosphodiester bond.) Tj
T*
(   * The excised intron is released as a free Lariat RNA, which is rapidly linearized by the) Tj
T*
(   debranching enzyme \(DBR1\) and degraded by nuclear ribonucleases.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Spliceosome as a Ribozyme:) Tj
T*
(   High-resolution cryo-EM structures demonstrate that the spliceosome is an authentic RNA-based) Tj
T*
(   catalytic enzyme \(Ribozyme\):) Tj
T*
(   - U2 and U6 snRNAs base-pair into an intricate secondary structure coordinating two catalytic) Tj
T*
(   divalent Magnesium ions \(Mg2+ A and Mg2+ B\).) Tj
T*
(   - The U2/U6 RNA network perfectly mirrors the active-site catalytic domain V of self-splicing) Tj
T*
(   Group II introns, proving that eukaryotic nuclear splicing is catalytically homologous to) Tj
T*
(   ancient self-splicing ribozymes.) Tj
