T*
(   4. Clinical Example \(SMN1/SMN2 and Spinal Muscular Atrophy\):) Tj
T*
(   - Humans have two near-identical genes: SMN1 \(telomeric\) and SMN2 \(centromeric\).) Tj
T*
(   - A single silent C-to-T transition in exon 7 of SMN2 \(c.840C>T\) disrupts an SF2/ASF ESE while) Tj
T*
(   creating an hnRNP A1 ESS silencer.) Tj
T*
(   - This causes 90% of SMN2 transcripts to skip exon 7, producing a truncated, unstable SMNDelta7) Tj
T*
(   protein.) Tj
T*
(   - Deletion of SMN1 leads to Spinal Muscular Atrophy \(SMA\), the leading genetic cause of infant) Tj
T*
(   death.) Tj
T*
(   - The therapeutic antisense oligonucleotide Nusinersen \(Spinraza\) binds to an ISS silencer in) Tj
T*
(   intron 7 of SMN2, physically displacing hnRNP A1, restoring exon 7 inclusion and producing) Tj
T*
(   therapeutic levels of full-length SMN protein.) Tj
