(   - When elongating RNA Polymerase II encounters a bulky DNA photoproduct \(e.g., UV-induced CPD\)) Tj
T*
(   on the template strand, the lesion cannot enter the catalytic active site cleft.) Tj
T*
(   - Pol II stalls irreversibly, occluding ~35 base pairs of DNA around the lesion, paradoxically) Tj
T*
(   preventing the standard GG-NER sensor \(XPC\) from gaining access.) Tj
T*
(   3. Recruitment of Cockayne Syndrome Proteins \(CSB and CSA\):) Tj
T*
(   - Stalled Pol II is recognized by Cockayne Syndrome Protein B \(CSB / ERCC6\):) Tj
T*
(   CSB is an SWI/SNF-like ATP-dependent chromatin remodeler that binds tightly to the upstream) Tj
T*
(   face of stalled Pol II and wraps adjacent DNA.) Tj
T*
