T*
(   CSA is a WD40-repeat protein functioning as part of a cullin-RING E3 ubiquitin ligase complex) Tj
T*
(   \(CRL4-CSA\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Backtracking and Core Machinery Recruitment:) Tj
T*
(   - CSB and CSA recruit the histone acetyltransferase p300 and the multi-protein complex UVSSA) Tj
T*
(   \(UV-Stimulated Scaffold Protein A\).) Tj
T*
(   - UVSSA recruits the deubiquitinating enzyme USP7, which stabilizes CSB against proteasomal) Tj
T*
(   degradation.) Tj
T*
(   - Working cooperatively, these factors remodel stalled Pol II, inducing reverse translocation) Tj
T*
(   \(backtracking\) by ~10 base pairs, or facilitating Pol II ubiquitination and removal, thereby) Tj
T*
(   exposing the buried DNA lesion.) Tj
T*
(   - TFIIH is directly recruited to the site independently of XPC.) Tj
T*
(   - XPA, RPA, XPG, and XPF-ERCC1 execute the standard dual incisions, excising the damaged 24-30) Tj
T*
(   nt oligonucleotide, followed by gap repair synthesis by Pol delta/epsilon and ligation.) Tj
