(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Mismatch Repair \(MMR\) pathway in E. coli, highlighting the roles of MutS, MutL, MutH, and Dam methylase in strand discrimination.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mismatch Repair \(MMR\) in Escherichia coli:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Fidelity Challenge:) Tj
T*
(   Post-replicative mismatch repair must recognize base-base mispairs \(e.g., G-T, A-C\) and small) Tj
T*
(   insertion-deletion loops \(indels\) that escape DNA Polymerase III proofreading. Crucially, the) Tj
T*
(   repair machinery must accurately discriminate the nascent error-containing daughter strand from) Tj
T*
(   the parental template strand!) Tj
T*
(   2. Strand Discrimination via Dam Methylase Hemimethylation:) Tj
T*
(   - E. coli possesses Dam Methylase \(Deoxyadenosine Methylase\), which constitutively methylates) Tj
T*
(   the N-6 position of adenine in symmetric 5'-GATC-3' sequences.) Tj
T*
(   - Immediately following the passage of the replication fork, the parental strand retains its) Tj
T*
(   GATC methyl groups, but newly synthesized daughter DNA is unmethylated.) Tj
T*
(   - For a transient temporal window of ~1-2 minutes, the newly replicated DNA is Hemimethylated) Tj
T*
(   \(methylated on the parental strand only\).) Tj
T*
(   3. The MutS - MutL - MutH Execution Cascade:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Mismatch Recognition\): The MutS homodimer scans duplex DNA. Upon encountering a) Tj
T*
(   mismatch, it kinks the DNA by 60 degrees. ATP binding induces MutS to adopt a closed sliding) Tj
T*
(   clamp conformation that diffuses along the DNA.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Matchmaker MutL\): MutS recruits the MutL homodimer \(an ATP-dependent molecular) Tj
T*
(   matchmaker\), assembling a ternary MutS-MutL-DNA complex.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Strand-Specific Incision by MutH\): MutS-MutL activates the sequence-specific) Tj
T*
(   endonuclease MutH. MutH binds specifically to hemimethylated 5'-GATC-3' sites.) Tj
T*
(   Activated MutH selectively introduces a single-strand nick into the unmethylated daughter) Tj
T*
(   strand 5' to the G of the GATC sequence, leaving the methylated parental strand intact!) Tj
T*
(   4. Excision and Resynthesis:) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Helicase II \(UvrD\) unwinds the nicked daughter strand from the GATC site through the) Tj
T*
(   mismatch.) Tj
T*
