(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how human Mismatch Repair operates without hemimethylation, detailing MSH/MLH complexes and nick-directed exonucleolytic excision.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Human Mismatch Repair \(MMR\) and Strand Discrimination Without Dam Methylase:) Tj
T*
(   1. Eukaryotic Mismatch Recognition Complexes:) Tj
T*
(   Human MMR utilizes specialized heterodimers of MutS and MutL homologs:) Tj
T*
(   - MutS-alpha \(MSH2 - MSH6 Heterodimer\): Abundant complex recognizing single base-base mispairs) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., G-T\) and small 1-nucleotide insertion-deletion loops.) Tj
T*
(   - MutS-beta \(MSH2 - MSH3 Heterodimer\): Specializes in recognizing larger insertion-deletion) Tj
T*
(   loops \(2 to 8 nucleotides\) resulting from replication slippage across microsatellites.) Tj
T*
(   2. The MutL Complexes:) Tj
T*
(   - MutL-alpha \(MLH1 - PMS2 Heterodimer\): The primary functional endonuclease partner.) Tj
T*
(   - MutL-beta \(MLH1 - PMS1\) and MutL-gamma \(MLH1 - MLH3\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Eukaryotic Strand Discrimination Mechanism \(The Pre-Existing Nick Paradigm\):) Tj
T*
(   Eukaryotes lack a functional equivalent of Dam methylase. Instead, strand discrimination relies) Tj
T*
(   directly on physical structural landmarks naturally present during DNA replication:) Tj
T*
(   - On the Lagging Strand: Transient unligated nicks and gaps between adjacent Okazaki fragments) Tj
T*
(   provide inherent, natural strand discrimination landmarks marking the newly synthesized) Tj
T*
(   daughter strand.) Tj
T*
(   - On the Leading Strand: Asymmetric loading of the PCNA sliding clamp by RFC establishes an) Tj
T*
(   oriented structural vector directing repair. In addition, transient ribonucleotides) Tj
T*
(   misincorporated by replicative polymerases \(~1 per 1,000 bp\) are nicked by RNase H2, providing) Tj
T*
(   strand markers.) Tj
T*
(   4. Latent Endonuclease Activation and Excision:) Tj
T*
(   - MSH2-MSH6 binds a mismatch, consumes ATP to form a sliding clamp, and recruits MLH1-PMS2.) Tj
T*
(   - The PMS2 subunit possesses a latent metal-dependent endonuclease active site \(DQHA\(X\)2E\(X\)4E) Tj
T*
(   motif\).) Tj
T*
(   - Interaction with PCNA and MutS-alpha activates the PMS2 endonuclease, which introduces) Tj
T*
(   single-strand nicks into the newly synthesized daughter strand near the mismatch.) Tj
T*
(   - Exonuclease 1 \(EXO1\): Recruited to the nick, EXO1 executes processive 5'-to-3' excision to) Tj
T*
(   digest the daughter strand past the mismatch.) Tj
T*
(   - RPA coats the gap; DNA Polymerase delta resynthesizes the DNA with high fidelity; DNA Ligase) Tj
T*
(   I seals the nick.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
