T*
(   3. Physiological Purpose:) Tj
T*
(   Maintains promoters in an open, nucleosome-free configuration, primed for instantaneous,) Tj
T*
(   synchronous, genome-wide transcriptional activation in response to heat shock, hormone pulses,) Tj
T*
(   or developmental signals.) Tj
T*
(   4. The P-TEFb Release Switch:) Tj
T*
(   - Upon receipt of activating signals, the positive elongation factor P-TEFb \(Positive) Tj
T*
(   Transcription Elongation Factor b, composed of Cyclin T1 and CDK9\) is recruited to paused) Tj
T*
(   promoters by transcription factors \(e.g., c-Myc, NF-kappa-B\) or the Super Elongation Complex) Tj
T*
(   \(SEC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Active CDK9 executes three coordinated phosphorylation events:) Tj
T*
(   * Phosphorylates the NELF-E subunit: Phosphorylation introduces negative charges, causing NELF) Tj
T*
(   to dissociate completely from Pol II into the nucleoplasm.) Tj
T*
(   * Phosphorylates the C-terminal repeat domain of Spt5 \(DSIF\): Phosphorylation converts DSIF) Tj
T*
(   from a negative repressor into a powerful POSITIVE elongation factor that travels with Pol II.) Tj
T*
(   * Phosphorylates Serine-2 of the RNA Pol II CTD: Shifts Pol II into productive, high-velocity) Tj
T*
(   elongation \(> 2-3 kb/minute\) and licenses co-transcriptional splicing.) Tj
