(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the molecular mechanism of Rho-Dependent Transcription Termination in prokaryotes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mechanisms of Rho-Dependent Transcription Termination:) Tj
T*
(   1. Molecular Architecture of Rho Factor:) Tj
T*
(   Rho factor is a ring-shaped, homohexameric molecular motor belonging to the RecA/AAA+) Tj
T*
(   superfamily of ATP-dependent helicases:) Tj
T*
(   - Each 47 kDa subunit possesses an N-terminal primary RNA-binding domain \(PBS\) that binds) Tj
T*
(   single-stranded cytosine-rich RNA, and a C-terminal secondary RNA-binding domain containing the) Tj
T*
(   catalytic ATPase active site.) Tj
T*
(   - The hexamer forms an open, lock-washer-like ring with a central 12 A pore, through which) Tj
T*
(   single-stranded RNA threads.) Tj
T*
(   2. Recognition of the Rut Site:) Tj
T*
(   - Rho does not bind structured or translating RNA.) Tj
T*
(   - It specifically recognizes an unstructured, single-stranded RNA segment on nascent) Tj
T*
(   transcripts termed the Rut Site \(Rho utilization site\):) Tj
T*
(   * Length: Typically 70 to 80 nucleotides long.) Tj
T*
(   * Composition: Unusually rich in Cytosine residues \(~30-40%\) and poor in Guanine residues,) Tj
T*
(   preventing the formation of stable secondary hairpins.) Tj
T*
(   3. Translocation and ATP-Driven Motor Action:) Tj
T*
(   - Binding of the rut site into the primary binding sites on the outer face of the hexamer) Tj
T*
(   induces closing of the ring around the RNA strand.) Tj
T*
(   - Activated by RNA binding, the six ATPase active sites hydrolyze ATP sequentially around the) Tj
T*
(   ring.) Tj
T*
(   - Rho translocates processively along the single-stranded RNA in the 5'-to-3' direction,) Tj
T*
(   reeling in RNA and chasing after the elongating RNA polymerase at speeds of ~60) Tj
T*
(   nucleotides/second.) Tj
T*
(   4. Termination at the Pause Site:) Tj
T*
