12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structural mechanics of the Spliceosome Catalytic Activation \(B to B* and C complexes\) driven by DEXD/H-Box RNA Helicases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Spliceosome Assembly Dynamics and DExD/H-Box Helicase Activation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Stepwise Pre-Spliceosome Assembly \(E and A Complexes\):) Tj
T*
(   - Complex E \(Early / Commitment\): U1 snRNP binds the 5' splice site; splicing factor SF1/BBP) Tj
T*
(   binds the branch point; U2AF65 binds the polypyrimidine tract; U2AF35 binds the 3' AG) Tj
T*
(   dinucleotide.) Tj
T*
(   - Complex A \(Pre-Spliceosome\): U2 snRNP replaces SF1 at the branch point sequence, driven by) Tj
T*
(   ATP-dependent remodeling by the DEAD-box helicase Prp5.) Tj
T*
(   2. Tri-snRNP Integration \(Complex B\):) Tj
T*
(   The pre-assembled U4/U6.U5 Tri-snRNP joins Complex A to assemble the fully loaded, but) Tj
T*
(   catalytically dormant, Complex B.) Tj
T*
(   3. Activation Remodeling Driven by Brr2 \(B to B* Transition\):) Tj
T*
(   The catalytic core cannot form because the catalytic domain of U6 snRNA is held inactive in an) Tj
T*
(   intermolecular duplex with U4 snRNA:) Tj
T*
(   - The DExH-box helicase Brr2 binds U4 snRNA.) Tj
T*
(   - Powered by ATP hydrolysis, Brr2 processively unwinds the extensive base-pairing between U4) Tj
T*
(   and U6 snRNAs.) Tj
T*
(   - U4 snRNP is ejected from the spliceosome.) Tj
T*
(   - Concurrently, the DEAD-box helicase Prp28 uncouples U1 snRNP from the 5' splice site,) Tj
T*
(   allowing U6 snRNA to base-pair with the 5' splice site.) Tj
T*
(   - U6 snRNA folds into an intramolecular stem-loop \(ISL\) that base-pairs with U2 snRNA,) Tj
T*
(   assembling the catalytic RNA active-site core coordinating two catalytic Mg2+ ions, yielding) Tj
T*
(   the activated Complex B*.) Tj
T*
(   4. Catalytic Execution \(Complex C\):) Tj
T*
(   - The DEAH-box helicase Prp2 remodels Complex B*, allowing the 2'-OH of the branch point) Tj
T*
(   adenosine to execute the first transesterification, generating Complex C \(containing Exon 1 and) Tj
T*
(   the Lariat-Exon 2 intermediate\).) Tj
T*
(   - The DEAH-box helicase Prp16 then rearranges the active site, toggling it from the branching) Tj
T*
(   conformation to the exon ligation conformation.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 transesterification ligates the exons.) Tj
T*
(   - Finally, the DEAH-box helicases Prp22 and Prp43 utilize ATP hydrolysis to release the spliced) Tj
T*
(   mRNA and dismantle the post-splicing complex, recycling snRNPs for future rounds.) Tj
T*
