(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the molecular mechanism of Homologous Recombination mediated by the RecBCD pathway and RecA in Escherichia coli.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The RecBCD - RecA Homologous Recombination Pathway in E. coli:) Tj
T*
(   1. Double-Strand Break Processing by RecBCD:) Tj
T*
(   The RecBCD heterotrimeric complex \(~330 kDa\) is a bipolar molecular machine possessing dual) Tj
T*
(   helicase and nuclease activities:) Tj
T*
(   - RecB: A 3'-to-5' directed ATP-dependent DNA helicase that harbors the single nuclease domain.) Tj
T*
(   - RecD: A fast, 5'-to-3' directed ATP-dependent DNA helicase.) Tj
T*
(   - RecC: The central structural scaffold that splits the incoming duplex into two single) Tj
T*
(   strands.) Tj
T*
(   2. Fast Unwinding and Chi Site Recognition:) Tj
T*
(   - RecBCD binds blunt or nearly blunt DSBs, unwinding DNA at speeds > 1,000 bp/second.) Tj
T*
(   - Because RecD moves faster than RecB, the RecB nuclease predominantly degrades the 3'-terminal) Tj
T*
(   strand into small fragments.) Tj
T*
(   - Unwinding continues until RecC encounters an invariant octanucleotide sequence in the DNA:) Tj
T*
(   the Chi Site \(Crossover Hotspot Instigator: 5'-GCTGGTGG-3'\).) Tj
T*
(   3. The Allosteric Switch at Chi:) Tj
T*
(   - Recognition of Chi halts the motor momentarily and induces an allosteric conformational) Tj
T*
(   rearrangement:) Tj
T*
(   * The fast RecD helicase subunit is uncoupled or inactivated.) Tj
T*
(   * The nuclease activity of RecB is switched: it ceases degradation of the 3'-strand, while) Tj
T*
(   switching to degrade the 5'-strand!) Tj
T*
(   * The continuing 3'-to-5' translocation of RecB generates an intact, single-stranded 3' DNA) Tj
T*
(   tail terminating precisely at the Chi site.) Tj
T*
(   4. RecA Nucleofilament Assembly and Strand Exchange:) Tj
T*
(   - RecBCD directly loads the bacterial recombinase RecA onto the newly generated single-stranded) Tj
T*
(   3'-tail, preventing SSB inhibition.) Tj
T*
(   - RecA polymerizes into a helical nucleoprotein filament \(6 RecA monomers per turn\) that) Tj
T*
(   stretches the ssDNA by 50%.) Tj
T*
(   - The RecA filament scans intact homologous duplex DNA, pairing to form a three-stranded) Tj
T*
(   intermediate \(paranemic joint\), followed by strand exchange to form a stable plectonemic) Tj
T*
(   heteroduplex \(D-loop\).) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Polymerase I extends the 3'-end; RuvAB branch-migrates the Holliday junctions, and RuvC) Tj
T*
(   resolvase endonucleolytically cleaves the junctions to yield recombinant chromosomes.) Tj
T*
