(   The Mediator Multi-Subunit Coactivator Complex:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture of Mediator:) Tj
T*
(   Mediator is a massive \(~1.4 MDa\), conserved multiprotein coactivator complex consisting of 26) Tj
T*
(   to 30 distinct subunits organized into four modular structural domains:) Tj
T*
(   - Head Module: Directly contacts the unphosphorylated C-terminal domain \(CTD\) of RNA Polymerase) Tj
T*
(   II, TBP, and TFIIB.) Tj
T*
(   - Middle Module: Forms an extensive structural bridge contacting Pol II subunits Rpb4/Rpb7 and) Tj
T*
(   TFIIE.) Tj
T*
(   - Tail Module: Consists of the most evolutionarily divergent subunits \(Med15, Med16, Med23\),) Tj
T*
(   serving as the physical sensor that directly binds diverse sequence-specific transcription) Tj
T*
(   factor activation domains.) Tj
T*
(   - Transient CDK8 Kinase Module \(CDK8, Cyclin C, Med12, Med13\): Reversibly associates with) Tj
T*
(   Mediator, functioning predominantly as a transcriptional repressor by sterically occluding Pol) Tj
T*
(   II interaction and phosphorylating Cyclin H of TFIIH.) Tj
T*
(   2. Molecular Function as a Molecular Conduit:) Tj
T*
(   - Sequence-specific transcription factors \(activators\) bound to distal enhancers \(> 50 kb away\)) Tj
T*
(   loop across chromatin to contact specific subunits in the Mediator Tail \(e.g., SREBP binds) Tj
T*
(   Med15; nuclear hormone receptors bind Med1\).) Tj
T*
(   - This binding induces cooperative conformational rearrangements that propagate from the Tail) Tj
T*
(   through the Middle module to the Head module.) Tj
T*
(   - The rearranged Head module binds with high affinity to RNA Polymerase II, stabilizing its) Tj
T*
(   assembly into the Pre-Initiation Complex \(PIC\) and stimulating TFIIH-dependent open complex) Tj
T*
(   formation.) Tj
T*
(   3. Transcriptional Re-Initiation Scaffolding:) Tj
T*
(   Upon promoter clearance, Pol II escapes into elongation, but the Mediator complex remains) Tj
T*
(   docked at the promoter alongside TFIID, forming a stable 'Scaffold' that recruits subsequent) Tj
T*
(   rounds of RNA Polymerase II molecules, driving rapid transcriptional re-initiation.) Tj
T*
