12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the structural organization of Nucleosomes and explain how Histone Acetylation and Methylation regulate chromatin accessibility.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Nucleosome Structure and the Epigenetic Histone Code:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Nucleosome Core Particle \(NCP\) Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   The fundamental repeating unit of eukaryotic chromatin is the nucleosome:) Tj
T*
(   - Histone Octamer Core: Composed of a central \(H3-H4\)2 heterotetramer flanked by two H2A-H2B) Tj
T*
(   heterodimers.) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Wrapping: Exactly 147 base pairs of double-stranded DNA wrap 1.65 left-handed) Tj
T*
(   superhelical turns around the outer protein surface of the octamer core.) Tj
T*
(   - Structural Histones: Small, highly basic proteins rich in lysine and arginine \(> 20% of amino) Tj
T*
(   acids\). Their flexible, unstructured N-terminal 'tails' project outward through the DNA gyres) Tj
T*
(   into the nucleoplasm.) Tj
T*
(   - Linker DNA and Histone H1: 20 to 80 base pairs of linker DNA separate adjacent nucleosomes) Tj
T*
(   \('beads-on-a-string'\). The linker histone H1 binds the entry/exit DNA sites, condensing 11 nm) Tj
T*
(   fibers into 30 nm chromatin fibers.) Tj
T*
(   2. Histone Acetylation \(The Open Euchromatin State\):) Tj
T*
(   - Catalyzed by Histone Acetyltransferases \(HATs, e.g., p300/CBP, Gcn5\); reversed by Histone) Tj
T*
(   Deacetylases \(HDACs\).) Tj
T*
(   - Targets: The epsilon-amino groups of conserved lysine residues on H3 and H4 tails \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   H3K9ac, H3K14ac, H4K16ac\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanism: Acetylation neutralizes the positive charge of the lysine ammonium group \(-NH3+ ->) Tj
T*
(   -NH-COCH3\). This abolishes electrostatic attraction between histone tails and the negatively) Tj
T*
(   charged DNA phosphate backbone, loosening the nucleosome.) Tj
T*
