12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the molecular mechanisms of Transcription Termination in Eukaryotes, contrasting the Allosteric \(Conformational\) and Torpedo models.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mechanisms of Eukaryotic RNA Polymerase II Transcription Termination:) Tj
T*
(   1. The 3'-End Processing Landmark:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike prokaryotes, eukaryotic RNA Polymerase II transcribes hundreds to thousands of) Tj
T*
(   nucleotides past the polyadenylation cleavage site before terminating. Termination is triggered) Tj
T*
(   when the polymerase transcribes the bipartite core polyadenylation signal: the AAUAAA hexamer) Tj
T*
(   followed by a downstream GU-rich element.) Tj
T*
(   2. Model 1: The Allosteric \(Conformational Change\) Model:) Tj
T*
(   - Proposes that transcription of the polyadenylation signal triggers an intrinsic structural) Tj
T*
(   remodeling of RNA Polymerase II:) Tj
T*
(   - As Pol II transcribes the AAUAAA signal, positive elongation factors \(e.g., Spt5, P-TEFb\)) Tj
T*
(   dissociate from the complex, while cleavage factors \(CPSF, CstF\) transfer from the CTD to the) Tj
T*
(   nascent RNA.) Tj
T*
(   - Concurrently, dephosphorylation of Ser-2 on the CTD alters the conformation of the catalytic) Tj
T*
(   cleft, dramatically reducing elongation processivity and destabilizing the 8-9 bp RNA-DNA) Tj
T*
(   hybrid in the active center.) Tj
T*
(   - The resulting conformational destabilization causes Pol II to spontaneously detach from the) Tj
T*
(   DNA template downstream.) Tj
T*
(   3. Model 2: The Torpedo Model \(The Enzymatic Chase\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Cleavage and Polyadenylation Specificity Factor \(CPSF-73 endonuclease\)) Tj
T*
(   endonucleolytically cleaves the nascent pre-mRNA at the CA dinucleotide site. The upstream) Tj
T*
(   capped mRNA is released for polyadenylation.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Cleavage leaves an uncapped 5'-monophosphate end on the downstream RNA fragment still) Tj
T*
(   emerging from the elongating RNA Polymerase II.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: This uncapped 5'-end is recognized by the nuclear 5'-to-3' exoribonuclease XRN2 \(Rat1) Tj
T*
(   in yeast\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: XRN2 acts as an enzymatic 'Torpedo': it processively degrades the nascent RNA in the) Tj
T*
(   5'-to-3' direction at high velocity \(> 250 nt/minute\), chasing down the advancing RNA) Tj
T*
(   Polymerase II.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: When XRN2 reaches the back of Pol II, it pulls the remaining RNA out of the catalytic) Tj
T*
(   cleft, disrupting the active site and terminating transcription.) Tj
T*
(   4. Modern Unified View:) Tj
T*
(   Current genome-wide empirical data indicate a Cooperative Hybrid Model: Allosteric) Tj
T*
(   conformational changes slow Pol II down at downstream pause sites, giving the XRN2 Torpedo) Tj
T*
ET

