(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the CRISPR-Cas9 bacterial adaptive immune system and detail how Cas9 introduces targeted double-strand breaks.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Type II CRISPR-Cas9 System and Targeted Genome Editing:) Tj
T*
(   1. Bacterial Adaptive Immunity:) Tj
T*
(   CRISPR \(Clustered Regularly Interspaced Short Palindromic Repeats\) and Cas \(CRISPR-associated\)) Tj
T*
(   proteins form an RNA-guided adaptive immune defense in bacteria \(e.g., Streptococcus pyogenes\)) Tj
T*
(   that captures, remembers, and destroys invading bacteriophage and plasmid DNA.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Dual-RNA Guide Complex:) Tj
T*
(   - CRISPR RNA \(crRNA\): Contains a 20-nucleotide variable spacer sequence complementary to the) Tj
T*
(   target foreign DNA \(protospacer\).) Tj
T*
(   - Trans-Activating crRNA \(tracrRNA\): Contains a sequence that base-pairs with the invariant) Tj
T*
(   repeat region of the crRNA, forming an RNA duplex that acts as a structural scaffold.) Tj
T*
(   - Single Guide RNA \(sgRNA\): In biotechnology, Jennifer Doudna and Emmanuelle Charpentier) Tj
T*
(   engineered an artificial chimera fusing crRNA and tracrRNA into a single ~100 nt guide RNA.) Tj
T*
(   3. Target Recognition and PAM Requirement:) Tj
T*
(   - Cas9 is a multi-domain endonuclease \(containing REC and NUC lobes\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cas9-sgRNA scans double-stranded DNA for a mandatory 2-6 base pair Protospacer Adjacent Motif) Tj
T*
(   \(PAM\). For S. pyogenes Cas9, the PAM is 5'-NGG-3'.) Tj
T*
(   - The PAM-Interacting \(PI\) domain of Cas9 binds the NGG PAM, inducing localized duplex melting) Tj
T*
(   immediately upstream.) Tj
T*
(   - The 20-nt spacer of the guide RNA interrogates the unzipped DNA target strand, forming an) Tj
T*
(   RNA-DNA hybrid \(R-loop\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Catalytic Cleavage Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   Once full 20-nt base pairing is verified, two distinct catalytic nuclease domains within Cas9) Tj
T*
(   execute double-strand cleavage:) Tj
T*
(   - HNH Endonuclease Domain: Cleaves the complementary \(target\) DNA strand 3 base pairs upstream) Tj
T*
(   of the PAM.) Tj
T*
(   - RuvC Endonuclease Domain: Cleaves the non-complementary \(non-target\) DNA strand 3 base pairs) Tj
T*
(   upstream of the PAM.) Tj
T*
(   - Yields a clean, blunt-ended Double-Strand Break \(DSB\) precisely at the target locus, which) Tj
T*
(   host repair machineries resolve via error-prone NHEJ \(introducing gene-disrupting indels\) or) Tj
T*
(   precise Homology-Directed Repair \(HDR\) using an exogenous donor template.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
