(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the molecular mechanism of Telomere Protection by the T-Loop and describe how TRF2 suppresses classical Non-Homologous End Joining.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   T-Loop Architecture and TRF2-Mediated Suppression of End-Joining:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Topological Architecture of the T-Loop:) Tj
T*
(   High-resolution electron microscopy and super-resolution STORM imaging reveal that mammalian) Tj
T*
(   telomeres do not exist as open linear duplexes; instead, the physical end of the chromosome) Tj
T*
(   folds back onto itself, forming a giant looped structure called the Telomeric Loop \(T-loop\):) Tj
T*
(   - At the base of the T-loop, the single-stranded 3' G-overhang \(150-300 nucleotides long\)) Tj
T*
(   invades the proximal double-stranded telomeric repeat array.) Tj
T*
(   - The invading G-strand base-pairs with the complementary C-rich strand, displacing the native) Tj
T*
(   G-strand into a single-stranded Displacement Loop \(D-loop\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Physical Masking Function:) Tj
T*
(   The T-loop configuration physically buries the vulnerable 3'-terminus inside the) Tj
T*
