T*
(   3. TRF2 as the Master Inhibitor of Classical NHEJ:) Tj
T*
(   - TRF2 binds with high affinity to double-stranded TTAGGG repeats via its C-terminal Myb) Tj
T*
(   domain.) Tj
T*
(   - Dimerization of TRF2 bends telomeric DNA by ~120 degrees, promoting the looping of the) Tj
T*
(   telomere back onto itself to facilitate T-loop formation.) Tj
T*
(   - Direct Ku70/80 Blockade: TRF2 physically blocks the Ku70/80 heterodimer from encircling the) Tj
T*
(   chromosome terminus.) Tj
T*
(   - ATM Kinase Inactivation: TRF2 possesses an N-terminal basic domain that directly binds the) Tj
T*
(   checkpoint sensor kinase ATM, locking it in an inactive, unphosphorylated state.) Tj
T*
(   4. Pathological Consequence of TRF2 Deletion:) Tj
T*
(   Experimental conditional knockout or dominant-negative inhibition of TRF2 causes instantaneous,) Tj
T*
(   catastrophic T-loop unravelling:) Tj
T*
(   - Chromosome ends are instantly recognized as authentic double-strand breaks.) Tj
T*
(   - Ku70/80 loads immediately onto every telomere end, recruiting DNA-PKcs and DNA Ligase IV.) Tj
T*
(   - Massive end-to-end chromosome fusions occur, ligating telomeres together to form giant) Tj
T*
(   multicentric ring and dicentric chromosomes.) Tj
T*
(   - In subsequent mitoses, dicentric chromosomes form anaphase bridges that shatter) Tj
T*
(   \(Breakage-Fusion-Bridge cycles\), driving massive genomic instability.) Tj
