12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the structure and mechanism of Group I and Group II Self-Splicing Introns, comparing their catalytic strategies to the nuclear Spliceosome.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Architecture and Catalytic Mechanisms of Self-Splicing Introns:) Tj
T*
(   1. Evolutionary Context \(The RNA World Hypothesis\):) Tj
T*
(   Self-splicing introns are catalytic RNAs \(Ribozymes\) found in bacterial genomes, mitochondrial) Tj
T*
(   and chloroplast genes, and lower eukaryotes that execute their own excision in vitro in the) Tj
T*
(   complete absence of any protein enzymes, providing strong evidence for an ancestral RNA-based) Tj
T*
(   biological world.) Tj
T*
(   2. Group I Self-Splicing Introns:) Tj
T*
(   - Structural Core: Highly conserved secondary structure consisting of nine paired stems \(P1 to) Tj
T*
(   P9\) organizing a central catalytic pocket.) Tj
T*
(   - Exogenous Nucleophile: Requires an exogenous guanosine cofactor \(free GTP, GDP, or GMP\) as) Tj
T*
(   the initial nucleophile.) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * Step 1: Free guanosine binds a specific pocket in stem P7. Its 3'-hydroxyl group \(3'-OH\)) Tj
T*
(   attacks the 5' splice site phosphodiester bond, becoming covalently attached to the 5' end of) Tj
T*
(   the excised intron.) Tj
T*
(   * Step 2: The liberated 3'-OH of the 5' exon attacks the 3' splice site, ligating the exons and) Tj
T*
(   releasing the linear intron with an extra G at its 5'-terminus.) Tj
T*
(   3. Group II Self-Splicing Introns:) Tj
T*
(   - Structural Core: Form an intricate six-domain cloverleaf structure \(Domains I through VI\)) Tj
T*
(   radiating from a central wheel. Domain V forms the catalytic active-site core, while Domain VI) Tj
T*
(   contains an invariant internal branch point Adenosine.) Tj
T*
(   - Endogenous Nucleophile: Uses the 2'-OH of its internal branch point Adenosine as the initial) Tj
T*
(   nucleophile \(identical to nuclear pre-mRNA splicing!\).) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * Step 1: The 2'-OH of the branch point adenosine attacks the 5' splice site, forming a) Tj
T*
(   branched 2'-5' phosphodiester bond, generating a Lariat intermediate.) Tj
T*
(   * Step 2: The 3'-OH of the 5' exon attacks the 3' splice site, ligating the exons and releasing) Tj
T*
(   the excised Lariat intron.) Tj
T*
