(   4. Structural Homology to the Nuclear Spliceosome:) Tj
T*
(   - Group II introns and the eukaryotic spliceosome are universally acknowledged to share direct) Tj
T*
(   common ancestry:) Tj
T*
(   * Both proceed via identical two-step transesterification chemistry using a 2'-OH branch point) Tj
T*
(   adenosine nucleophile to form a lariat intermediate.) Tj
T*
(   * The catalytic core of Domain V in Group II introns is structurally superimposable on the) Tj
T*
(   U2/U6 snRNA catalytic duplex in the activated spliceosome.) Tj
T*
(   * Over evolutionary time, the structural domains of ancient Group II introns fragmented in) Tj
T*
(   trans, evolving into the independent U1, U2, U4, U5, and U6 snRNAs, while the host cell) Tj
T*
(   supplied stabilizing proteins to form the modern spliceosome.) Tj
T*
